Pour développer une application client-serveur de sondage en Java, nous allons créer trois classes principales : `Sondage`, `Serveur`, et `Client`. Nous utiliserons un `Executor` pour gérer les requêtes simultanées des clients et assurer la synchronisation des votes.

### 1. Classe `Sondage`

Cette classe représente le sondage et gère les propositions, les votes, et le résultat.

```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class Sondage {
    private final List<String> propositions;
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, AtomicInteger> votes;

    public Sondage(List<String> propositions) {
        this.propositions = propositions;
        this.votes = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < propositions.size(); i++) {
            votes.put(i, new AtomicInteger(0));
        }
    }

    public List<String> getPropositions() {
        return propositions;
    }

    public String vote(int propositionIndex) {
        if (propositionIndex < 0 || propositionIndex >= propositions.size()) {
            return "ERR";
        }
        votes.get(propositionIndex).incrementAndGet();
        return "OK";
    }

    public String getResultat() {
        int maxIndex = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i < votes.size(); i++) {
            if (votes.get(i).get() > votes.get(maxIndex).get()) {
                maxIndex = i;
            }
        }
        return propositions.get(maxIndex);
    }
}
```

### 2. Classe `Serveur`

Cette classe gère les connexions des clients et utilise un `ExecutorService` pour traiter les requêtes de manière concurrente.

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.net.ServerSocket;
import java.net.Socket;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;

public class Serveur {
    private final int port;
    private final Sondage sondage;
    private final ExecutorService executor;

    public Serveur(int port, Sondage sondage) {
        this.port = port;
        this.sondage = sondage;
        this.executor = Executors.newCachedThreadPool();
    }

    public void start() throws IOException {
        try (ServerSocket serverSocket = new ServerSocket(port)) {
            System.out.println("Serveur démarré sur le port " + port);
            while (true) {
                Socket clientSocket = serverSocket.accept();
                executor.submit(new ClientHandler(clientSocket, sondage));
            }
        }
    }

    private static class ClientHandler implements Runnable {
        private final Socket socket;
        private final Sondage sondage;

        public ClientHandler(Socket socket, Sondage sondage) {
            this.socket = socket;
            this.sondage = sondage;
        }

        @Override
        public void run() {
            try (BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(socket.getInputStream()));
                 PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(socket.getOutputStream(), true)) {

                String request;
                while ((request = in.readLine()) != null) {
                    String response = handleRequest(request);
                    out.println(response);
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            } finally {
                try {
                    socket.close();
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    e.printStackTrace();
                }
            }
        }

        private String handleRequest(String request) {
            if (request.startsWith("candidats")) {
                return String.join(", ", sondage.getPropositions());
            } else if (request.startsWith("vote ")) {
                try {
                    int propositionIndex = Integer.parseInt(request.substring(5));
                    return sondage.vote(propositionIndex);
                } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
                    return "ERR";
                }
            } else if (request.equals("resultat")) {
                return sondage.getResultat();
            } else {
                return "ERR";
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        List<String> propositions = Arrays.asList("Proposition 1", "Proposition 2", "Proposition 3");
        Sondage sondage = new Sondage(propositions);
        Serveur serveur = new Serveur(12345, sondage);
        serveur.start();
    }
}
```

