To extract a specific piece of XML from a given XML string in Java, you can use the `javax.xml.parsers` and `org.w3c.dom` packages to parse the XML and then navigate the DOM tree to extract the desired element. Below is an example of how you can achieve this:

```java
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.NodeList;
import org.w3c.dom.Node;
import org.w3c.dom.Element;
import java.io.ByteArrayInputStream;
import javax.xml.transform.Transformer;
import javax.xml.transform.TransformerFactory;
import javax.xml.transform.dom.DOMSource;
import javax.xml.transform.stream.StreamResult;
import java.io.StringWriter;

public class XmlExtractor {

    public static String extractXmlPiece(String xmlString, String tagName) throws Exception {
        // Convert the XML string to a ByteArrayInputStream
        ByteArrayInputStream input = new ByteArrayInputStream(xmlString.getBytes("UTF-8"));

        // Parse the XML string into a Document
        DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
        DocumentBuilder builder = factory.newDocumentBuilder();
        Document document = builder.parse(input);

        // Normalize the XML structure
        document.getDocumentElement().normalize();

        // Get all elements with the specified tag name
        NodeList nodeList = document.getElementsByTagName(tagName);

        // Check if any elements were found
        if (nodeList.getLength() == 0) {
            return ""; // Return empty string if no elements found
        }

        // Get the first matching element
        Node node = nodeList.item(0);

        // Convert the Node to a String
        return nodeToString(node);
    }

    private static String nodeToString(Node node) throws Exception {
        StringWriter sw = new StringWriter();
        Transformer t = TransformerFactory.newInstance().newTransformer();
        t.transform(new DOMSource(node), new StreamResult(sw));
        return sw.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String xmlString = "<root><person><name>John Doe</name><age>30</age></person><person><name>Jane Doe</name><age>28</age></person></root>";
        try {
            String extractedXml = extractXmlPiece(xmlString, "person");
            System.out.println(extractedXml);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
1. **Parsing the XML**: The XML string is converted into a `ByteArrayInputStream` and then parsed into a `Document` object using `DocumentBuilder`.

2. **Extracting the Element**: The `getElementsByTagName` method is used to find all elements with the specified tag name. If elements are found, the first one is selected.

3. **Converting Node to String**: The `nodeToString` method converts the selected `Node` back into a string representation of the XML fragment using `Transformer`.

4. **Main Method**: The `main` method demonstrates how to use the `extractXmlPiece` method to extract and print the first `person` element from the XML string.

