Here’s a step-by-step solution to fix this issue:

### Step 1: Understand the Problem
The issue arises because `tagsText` is a single variable that is being appended to in each iteration of the loop. The functions inside `selectedTaggers.map` capture this variable by reference, so they all refer to the same `tagsText` that exists at the end of the loop, not the value it had at the time the function was created.

### Step 2: Isolate `tagsText` for Each Iteration
To fix this, you need to ensure that each iteration of the loop has its own isolated `tagsText` variable. You can achieve this by moving the `tagsText` initialization inside the loop or by using a different approach to accumulate the results.

### Step 3: Refactor the Code
Here’s the refactored version of your function:

```javascript
const performTagging = async (selected, source) => {
  if (selectedTaggers.length > 0) {
    try {
      let allTagsText = ""; // This will accumulate the final result

      for (const image of selectedImages) {
        let imageTagsText = `Image ${image.id}\n`; // Initialize tagsText for the current image

        const fetchTagPromises = selectedTaggers.map(async (tagger) => {
          try {
            const url = source === "Database"
              ? `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tags/db/${image.id}?hf_url=${encodeURIComponent(tagger.hf_url)}&model=${encodeURIComponent(tagger.model)}&tag_file=${encodeURIComponent(tagger.tag_file)}`
              : `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/tags/${image.id}?hf_url=${encodeURIComponent(tagger.hf_url)}&model=${encodeURIComponent(tagger.model)}&tag_file=${encodeURIComponent(tagger.tag_file)}`;

            const response = await axios.get(url);
            return { tagger: tagger.hf_url, tags: response.data };
          } catch (error) {
            console.error(`Error tagging image ${image.id} with tagger ${tagger.hf_url}: `, error.response || error.message || error);
            return { tagger: tagger.hf_url, tags: [], error: true };
          }
        });

        const taggerResults = await Promise.all(fetchTagPromises);

        taggerResults.forEach((result) => {
          if (!result.error) {
            const formattedTags = result.tags
              .map((tagObj) => {
                const tag = Object.keys(tagObj)[0];
                const score = Object.values(tagObj)[0];
                return `\t${tag}: ${score.toFixed(4)}`;
              })
              .join("\n");

            imageTagsText += `Tags by ${result.tagger}:\n{\n${formattedTags}\n}\n\n`;
