To avoid using regex lookback in your BBcode parser, you can modify the regex patterns and the logic that relies on them. Specifically, you can replace the lookbehind and lookahead assertions with alternative approaches that achieve the same result without relying on these features.

Here’s how you can modify the code to avoid using regex lookback:

### 1. **Replace Lookbehind/Lookahead with Capture Groups and Conditional Logic**

Instead of using lookbehind (`(?<=...)`) and lookahead (`(?=...)`), you can capture the relevant parts of the string and process them conditionally.

#### Example: `Patterns.getBreakLineBeforeTag` and `Patterns.getBreakLineAfterTag`

```javascript
class Patterns {
  // ... other methods ...

  static getBreakLineBeforeTag(tagTypes, flags = '') {
    const tags = Patterns.prepareTags(...tagTypes);
    // Original: /(?<=\[\/(.*?)\])\n+(?=\[\/(?:${tags})\])/
    // Replacement: Capture the closing tag and newline, then check the next tag
    return new RegExp(`\\[\\/(.*?)\\](\\n+)(\\[\\/?(?:${tags})\\])`, flags);
  }

  static getBreakLineAfterTag(tagTypes, flags = '') {
    const tags = Patterns.prepareTags(...tagTypes);
    // Original: /(?<=\[\/(?:${tags})\])\n/
    // Replacement: Capture the closing tag and newline
    return new RegExp(`\\[\\/?(?:${tags})\\](\\n)`, flags);
  }

  // ... other methods ...
}
```

Then, in the replacement logic, you can conditionally process the captured groups:

```javascript
