Yes, you can change the color of radio buttons in HTML and CSS, but it requires a bit of creativity since the default radio button styles are not directly customizable across all browsers. The most common approach is to hide the default radio button and create a custom design using CSS pseudo-elements. Here’s how you can do it:

### HTML
```html
<label class="custom-radio">
  <input type="radio" name="radio" value="1">
  <span class="radio-button"></span>
  Option 1
</label>

<label class="custom-radio">
  <input type="radio" name="radio" value="2">
  <span class="radio-button"></span>
  Option 2
</label>
```

### CSS
```css
/* Hide the default radio button */
.custom-radio input[type="radio"] {
  display: none;
}

/* Custom radio button design */
.custom-radio .radio-button {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  border: 2px solid #ccc; /* Default border color */
  border-radius: 50%;
  position: relative;
  margin-right: 10px;
  vertical-align: middle;
}

/* Style for the checked state */
.custom-radio input[type="radio"]:checked + .radio-button {
  border-color: #2196F3; /* Border color when checked */
}

/* Inner circle for the checked state */
.custom-radio input[type="radio"]:checked + .radio-button::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  background-color: #2196F3; /* Inner circle color when checked */
  border-radius: 50%;
}

/* Hover effect */
.custom-radio:hover .radio-button {
  border-color: #666; /* Border color on hover */
}
```

### Explanation:
1. **Hide Default Radio Button**: We hide the default radio button using `display: none;`.
2. **Custom Radio Button**: We create a custom radio button using a `<span>` element with the class `radio-button`. This span is styled to look like a radio button.
3. **Checked State**: When the radio button is checked, we change the border color and add an inner circle using the `::after` pseudo-element.
4. **Hover Effect**: We add a hover effect to change the border color when the user hovers over the radio button.

### Browser Compatibility:
This approach works across all modern browsers. However, keep in mind that the styling is completely custom, so it won’t inherit any browser-specific styles for radio buttons.

### Alternative Approach (Using `appearance: none`):
Some modern browsers support the `appearance: none;` property, which allows you to remove the default styling of the radio button and apply custom styles directly. However, this method is not supported in all browsers.

```css
input[type="radio"] {
  appearance: none;
  -webkit-appearance: none;
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  border: 2px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 50%;
